  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Why not through git",
      "items": [
        "The web UI cannot write to your repository — that needs write access to every repo, a bot, a commit per click",
        "A committed lockfile went stale the moment anyone clicked Add, then rewrote itself in every working tree",
        "Anyone with repo write could skip the scanner by editing a file"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "What git pull does, and the one-time setup",
      "items": [
        "git pull does nothing for skills — it fetches code. Sync happens at agent session start; `npx drymem skills pull` is the escape hatch",
        "`npx drymem setup` once per repo per machine installs the hook. Topics are tagged by the local model after publish, best effort",
        "An open session sees a new skill at its next restart — a post-merge hook would close that gap"
      ]
    }
  ]
